<title>BELGIUM: Antwerp port blocked by 24-hour strike.</title>
<headline>Antwerp port blocked by 24-hour strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian port of Antwerp, the second-biggest in Europe behind Rotterdam in the Netherlands, is completely blocked due to a 24-hour strike of port workers, the port authorities said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;All the locks are blocked by strikers. The entire port is blocked,&quot; a port authority spokesman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>He said some pilot services were working and that a few bridges were open, but that no traffic was possible because of the closure of the locks.</p>
<p>Port authority workers are striking in protest over a planned change in their status from public sector workers to private sector workers.</p>
<p>--Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810</p>
